{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q424767","formula":"C₄₄H₆₄O₂₄","hill":"C44H64O24","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":44.0,"H":64.0,"O":24.0},"names":{"en":"Crocin","ru":"Кроцин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Crocin is a carotenoid chemical compound that is found in the flowers of crocus, gardenia and Buddleja (butterfly bush) Crocin is the chemical primarily responsible for the color of saffron. Chemically, crocin is the diester formed from the disaccharide gentiobiose and the branched-chain dicarboxylic acid crocetin. When isolated as a pure chemical compound, it has a deep red color and forms crystals with a melting point of 186 °C. When dissolved in water, it forms an orange solution.","ru":"Кроцин — органическое соединение каротиноид, содержащееся в цветках растений рода Шафран (крокус) и Гардения. Он является основным пигментом, придающим шафрану его характерный ярко‑красный цвет."},"fame":21,"pubchemCid":5281233,"mass":977.0,"charge":0,"smiles":"C/C(=C\\C=C\\C=C(\\C=C\\C=C(\\C(=O)O[C@@H]1O[C@@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@H]1O)O)O)CO[C@@H]2O[C@@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@H]2O)O)O)CO)/C)/C)/C=C/C=C(/C(=O)O[C@@H]3O[C@@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@H]3O)O)O)CO[C@@H]4O[C@@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@H]4O)O)O)CO)\\C","inchikey":"SEBIKDIMAPSUBY-RTJKDTQDSA-N","iupac":"bis[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-[[(2R,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxymethyl]oxan-2-yl] (2E,4E,6E,8E,10E,12E,14E)-2,6,11,15-tetramethylhexadeca-2,4,6,8,10,12,14-heptaenedioate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"5281233","atoms":132,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.721,"y":2.532,"z":-2.896,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.478,"y":1.689,"z":-1.899,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.909,"y":0.793,"z":-1.063,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.502,"y":0.465,"z":-0.938,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.061,"y":-0.51,"z":-0.125,"el":"C"},